{
  "$schema": "../scene.schema.json",
  "id": "knot-inner",
  "name": "The Knot: Horn's Hall, the Fold, the Cradle and the Shaft's foot",
  "description": "Bead mw-e26.10: the inner half of the labyrinth as one connected greybox (about 100 x 175 m, one level). Through the Chapel landing (knot-outer horns-door, back to knot-outer arrive-from-knot-inner; arrive-from-knot-outer) a vestibule opens into Horn's Hall (horns-hall): an 80 x 60 m arena, 9 m tall, with pillars, four Hornfolk statues with their hands over their ears and Horn's post (horn-post; the Warden encounter is mw-e26.16). In the hall's west wall a doorway (fold-door) leads to the Fold (the-fold): a dead-end vault with six moss-bed markers and the chalk tallies, the one door of the respawn design. A second west doorway runs to the sealed crypt passage (crypt-passage, crypt-door locked with the priory's crypt-sealed lock, crypt-passage-end beyond it) that will rise to Bellwater Priory (mw-e26.20). North, a corridor (cradle-gate) leads to the Cradle (the-cradle): a 48 m chamber ringed by sixteen pillars with eight carved faces turned inward, the abbot's stage at the centre (cradle-centre, mw-e26.17), the last friend-below note and a doorway in the north wall to the Sounding Shaft's foot (sounding-shaft-foot; shaft-mouth, the climb is mw-e26.18). A secret way (route:horns-hall-cradle-secret) leaves the hall's east wall through a stone door sealed with a Hornfolk seal (hornfolk-door, lock hornfolk-seal, the runes of hornfolk-wall beside it) and runs round to the Cradle's east doorway (cradle-east-door): a wall until the seal is dispelled.",
  "grid": 1,
